  <p style="letter-spacing:2px;font-size:0.8em;color:#c9a84c;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;"><strong>The HOBOT Lineup, Explained</strong></p>
  <h2 style="color:#232739;font-size:1.8em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:20px;">Robots for the Cleaning Jobs Robots Usually Skip</h2>

  <p>Most home cleaning robots handle carpet and hard floors. Almost none of them climb glass, and the ones that mop floors properly, rather than just dragging a damp pad behind a vacuum, are rarer still. HOBOT Technology builds both: window-climbing robots that spray, scrub, and squeegee glass on their own, and the LEGEE-688, a 4-in-1 floor robot that vacuums and mops in a single pass instead of treating mopping as an afterthought.</p>

  <p>Yard Automation Pros carries three active HOBOT models: the HOBOT-2S and HOBOT-298 window cleaning robots, and the LEGEE-688 floor robot. The two window robots solve the same problem at two different levels of capability, and the LEGEE-688 solves a different problem entirely, so picking the right one starts with knowing which job you're actually trying to hand off.</p>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/hobot-2s-08-site.jpg?v=1789118947" alt="HOBOT-2S window cleaning robot cleaning glass" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 24px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900">

  <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;margin:48px 0 0;">
  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:48px;">HOBOT-2S: The Premium Window Robot</h3>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/hobot-2s-13-site.jpg?v=1789118947" alt="HOBOT-2S dual ultrasonic spray nozzles detail" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 20px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900">

  <p>The HOBOT-2S is HOBOT's most advanced window cleaning robot, and the gap between it and the 298 comes down to spray and coverage. Where the 298 has one spray nozzle, the 2S has two, spraying in three directions at once, roughly mimicking how a person's breath fogs and clears glass, but automated and continuous. Both produce a 15-micrometer mist fine enough to dissolve dust without leaving watermarks, but the 2S's dual-nozzle system covers more surface area per pass.</p>

  <p>The bigger practical difference is edge and corner handling. The 2S's 4X Edge-Leakage sensors detect air leakage from even a slight lift at a window seal or frameless edge, more precise than the laser-based detection on the 298, and its enlarged cleaning cloth reaches 80% corner coverage, double the 298's 40%. For large glass walls, frameless windows, or homes where thorough edge-to-edge cleaning matters more than base price, the 2S is the stronger choice. It also carries a heavier-rated 200 Kgf safety rope and the same 20-minute UPS emergency backup power as the 298, so a mid-cycle power interruption never leaves it stranded on the glass.</p>

  <p>Cleaning speed is 1 square meter per 2.4 minutes, using a two-pass zigzag-then-N-way pattern for full coverage, and it's controlled through the HOBOT app over Bluetooth, with OTA firmware updates and multilingual voice status prompts along the way.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">HOBOT-298: The Original, Still the Flagship Value</h3>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/hobot-298-amz-05.jpg?v=1773893651" alt="HOBOT-298 window cleaning robot" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 20px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900">

  <p>The HOBOT-298 is built around HOBOT's original Bio-mimicry Ultrasonic Water Spray, a patented 108KHz ultrasonic nozzle that nebulizes water into the same 15-micrometer mist used across the lineup, and it was a CES 2019 Innovation Awards honoree for exactly that system. Its AI Smart Route Plan runs the same two-pass zigzag-then-N-shaped cleaning cycle as the 2S, with auto edge detection handling frameless windows via dual laser sensors that measure distance and height for accurate boundary tracking.</p>

  <p>A 6.0 kg-force vacuum suction system, powered by a Nidec brushless motor with a metal fan, holds the robot firmly to the glass at a quiet 64 decibels, while an auto-adjustable pneumatic pad keeps tread pressure proportional so a dirty or uneven pane doesn't stall the cleaning cycle. It carries the same 20-minute UPS backup power as the 2S, ties off with a 4.5-meter, 150 Kgf-rated safety rope, and reaches up to 5 meters from an outlet using its included 4-meter extension cord. For most standard residential windows, the 298 delivers the same core spray-and-clean result as the 2S at a lower price, with the 2S's advantage concentrated specifically in corner coverage and edge-leakage sensitivity.</p>

