  <p>Both robots use the same core ultrasonic spray-and-clean approach, work on windows, tiled walls, frosted glass, and other smooth vertical surfaces, require a minimum window size of 40&times;40 cm, and control through the HOBOT app plus an included remote. If your glass includes large frameless panes or tricky corners, the 2S's extra sensor coverage earns its price gap. For standard framed residential windows, the 298 delivers the same fundamental result for less.</p>

  <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;margin:48px 0 0;">
  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:48px;">LEGEE-688: 4-in-1 Floor Cleaning, Vacuum and Mop in One Pass</h3>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/LEGEE-688_04.jpg?v=1773896320" alt="LEGEE-688 4-in-1 vacuum mop robot" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 20px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900">

  <p>The LEGEE-688 solves a different problem than the window robots: hard-floor cleaning where mopping is treated as a real cleaning step, not an add-on. Its patented FastBrush system runs vacuum, dry mop, AI smart spray, and wet mop in a single pass, with the mopping cloth vibrating at 600 to 800 times per minute for active scrubbing rather than just dragging a damp pad across the floor. Temperature-controlled AI Smart Spray releases just enough water to dissolve stains without leaving puddles or a slip hazard behind.</p>

  <p>LEGEE® Smart Navigation fuses five sensor types, laser, encoder, gyro, e-compass, and position estimation, to build a real-time map and clean systematically in 4.4-by-4.4-meter sections rather than bouncing randomly. Seven Talent Clean modes, plus one fully customizable mode, cover different situations: Kitchen Mode makes two passes over greasy floor sections, first dissolving stubborn stains and then absorbing them; Pet Mode boosts vacuum and spray for pet hair and messes. A D-shaped body with a flat back edge and a 4 cm extended side brush reaches into corners and under cabinet edges that round robots miss entirely.</p>

  <p>A 500ml trash bin and 320ml water tank, good for roughly 150 square meters per fill, keep sessions running without frequent refills, and two-layer filtration, a washable 600-mesh screen plus a HEPA filter, catches both large debris and fine particles. The microfiber cloth cleaning system means no roller brush, and no roller brush means no hair tangling around it, a common failure point on cheaper floor robots. It's built for hard floors only, tile, wood, laminate, marble, glass, and epoxy, and isn't rated for carpet.</p>

