  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Robotic Cleaning vs. Doing It by Hand</h3>

  <p>Cleaning second-story exterior glass by hand usually means a squeegee, an extension pole, and either a ladder or a lot of careful leaning, none of which is a task most homeowners look forward to repeating every month. Mopping a full house of hard flooring by hand means a bucket, a mop head that redistributes as much dirty water as it picks up, and thirty minutes to an hour of bending and wringing.</p>

