  <p>Not sure which robot matches your home's windows or flooring? <a href="/pages/schedule-your-professional-consultation" style="color:#232739;font-weight:bold;">Book a free consultation</a> and we'll walk through your specific setup honestly, including telling you when the lower-priced option covers everything you need.</p>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/AA0I7211-2.jpg?v=1773896320" alt="LEGEE-688 cleaning hard floor" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 24px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900">

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Maintenance</h3>

  <p>The window robots use only HOBOT detergent or pure water in their spray tanks, hard water or other liquids can clog the ultrasonic nozzle over time, and the included microfiber cleaning cloths are washable and reusable. The LEGEE-688 uses a two-layer filtration system, a washable screen filter plus a replaceable HEPA filter, and its mopping cloths and spray nozzles are also replaceable, with spares included in the box. None of the three machines require any lubrication, belts, or motor maintenance beyond routine cleaning of their consumable parts.</p>

  <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;margin:48px 0 0;">
  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:48px;">Common Questions About the HOBOT Lineup</h3>

  <p><strong>Is it safe to use a window robot on the outside of a second-story window?</strong><br>
  Yes. Both window robots include a rated safety rope, 200 Kgf on the 2S and 150 Kgf on the 298, that ties off to an indoor fixture before the robot goes on the glass, and both carry 20 minutes of UPS backup power if the electrical supply is interrupted mid-cycle.</p>

  <p><strong>What's the real difference between the HOBOT-2S and HOBOT-298?</strong><br>
  Both use the same core ultrasonic spray-and-clean technology. The 2S adds a second spray nozzle, doubles corner coverage to 80%, and uses more precise edge-leakage sensors, at a higher price. The 298 delivers the same fundamental clean for less on standard framed windows.</p>

  <p><strong>Will the LEGEE-688 work on my carpet?</strong><br>
  No. It's built for hard floors only, tile, wood, laminate, marble, glass, and epoxy, and isn't rated for carpet.</p>

  <p><strong>What liquids can I use in the window robots?</strong><br>
  HOBOT detergent or pure water only. Other cleaning liquids can damage the ultrasonic spray nozzle.</p>

  <p><strong>Do these robots need Wi-Fi?</strong><br>
  The window robots connect via Bluetooth through the HOBOT app plus an included physical remote. The LEGEE-688 connects via Wi-Fi (802.11 b/g/n) through the HOBOT LEGEE app for full mapping, scheduling, and cleaning diary features.</p>

  <p><strong>What's the warranty?</strong><br>
  Warranty terms are listed on each individual product's specification sheet. Contact us if you need the exact coverage period for your specific model.</p>

  <p><strong>Can I finance a HOBOT robot?</strong><br>
  Yes, financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments across the HOBOT lineup.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Ownership, Handled</h3>

  <p>Every HOBOT robot is typically delivered in about two weeks. Financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments, so the cost spreads over time instead of landing as one lump sum. And you're not buying this from a manufacturer's storefront with no one to call, Yard Automation Pros provides real, US-based expert guidance before and after your purchase, from matching the right model to your home to helping you get the most out of it once it's running. If something isn't working the way it should, you have a real person to reach, not a support ticket queue.</p>

